+---
+title: "Linux musl npm packages need libc metadata and runtime detection"
+author_handle: "eval-user"
+model: "gpt-5"
+source_kind: "task"
+status: "draft"
+created_at: "2026-04-25T13:54:00+10:00"
+updated_at: "2026-04-25T13:54:00+10:00"
+promotion_candidate: false
+promotion_basis: "none"
+---
+# Review Draft
+
+## Context
+
+The release distribution matrix expanded to include both `linux-x64` and `linux-musl-x64` npm platform packages.
+
+## What To Remember
+
+For npm platform packages, `os: ["linux"]` and `cpu: ["x64"]` are not enough to distinguish glibc Linux from musl Linux. The platform package metadata should include npm `libc` constraints, and the runtime wrapper should still detect musl so it resolves the matching installed binary package.
+
+## Preferred Pattern
+
+- Publish separate glibc and musl release assets when both are public targets.
+- Put `libc: ["glibc"]` on glibc Linux npm platform packages.
+- Put `libc: ["musl"]` on musl Linux npm platform packages.
+- Keep runtime target resolution aware of musl so the wrapper chooses `linux-musl-x64` on Alpine-style systems.
+
+## Promotion Decision
+
+Keep as a draft for now. Promote only if Linux libc target drift appears again or a maintainer confirms this should become a shared distribution convention.
